WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.930
Draw a thirty degree angle at A.

2
00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:06.820
Mark C on one arm, ten centimetres from A.

3
00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:11.240
Now hang a six centimetre arm
from C, and let it swing down.

4
00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:13.290
It touches the line once.

5
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.940
Swinging further, it touches it again.

6
00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:20.320
Same sides, same angle, yet
two different triangles.

7
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.190
How?

8
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.340
Is one just a mirror image?

9
00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:28.570
In this mission, you'll label a
triangle so side a is opposite angle A.

10
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:35.010
You'll use the sine rule: a over sine A
equals b over sine B equals c over sine

11
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:35.840
C.

12
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:40.840
And you'll use the cosine rule, and
a sine formula for a triangle's area.

13
00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:46.520
Your mission: explain how two sides and
an angle can give two different triangles.
